  "jobTitle": "Software Engineer",
  "summary": "I've enjoyed a 22 year career at HP designing, developing, and delivering end to end scanning solutions across a wide range of HP products.  I've architected and implemented a cross HP scanning API that unified our OEM driver deliverables, allowing us to deliver single software solutions that work seamlessly across all devices.  My passion is solving tough problems with creative solutions.. I recently found and fixed an issue blocking a $10M hardware purchase contract, allowing HP to seal the deal.  \n\nMy career at HP begin as a test manager/lead for scan programs.   I moved quickly to a development role, and became an expert in developing APIs and drivers for a wide range of scanners.   I trained our ODM/OEM/HP partners in driver design and development.   I worked with Microsoft to improve their Windows scanning APIs, and to integrate our portfolio of scan driver solutions in-OS to improve customer install experience.  Speaking of customers, I also found my passion for customer satisfaction through active participation in customer forums.  I've championed many solutions to customer facing issues, and led our software teams to correct those issues in future software releases.\n\nMost recently I've been involved in scan and capture workflow app development, creating a first-of-its-kind Windows 8 modern app that delighted customers and received millions of downloads.  Following this was development of a cross platform (iOS/Android/UWP) workflow app using Xamarin that allowed for 60-70% code reuse, saving the company development time, resources, and test effort.   And currently my focus is on developing cloud based workflow solutions that will be used HP wide.\n\nI enjoy working on highly motivated teams, and collaborating with peers to make the impossible a reality.  I strive to continuously learn through research, failures, and the wisdom of others.   \n\nOutside of work you'll find me casting my worries to the wind with a fly-rod and fish laden waters.  ",
